  "style": "",
  "text": "In conclusion, the present study suggests that CRT-S may be associated with longer OS and PFS than D-CRT in T4 ESCC patients who were downstaged by neo-CRT, although these findings are preliminary and should be interpreted with caution. However, the present study did have several limitations. First, this was a retrospective study from a single institution. Second, half of the patients included in the study were staged as T4 by CT imaging and not by endoscopy. Furthermore, the number of patients included in the study was small. Randomized controlled trials involving large population samples are needed to define the standard treatment for T4 esophageal cancer."
}

